---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Article from "../layouts/Article.astro";
import mobile from "../assets/platform-mobile.webp";
import { go } from "../data/site";
const toc = [
  { id: "android", label: "Android" },
  { id: "iphone", label: "iPhone and iPad" },
  { id: "desktop", label: "Windows and macOS" },
  { id: "telegram", label: "Telegram bot" },
  { id: "compare", label: "Which one to use" },
];
---

<Article
  cover="app"
  title="Pocket Option App: Android, iPhone, PC and Telegram"
  description="How to get the Pocket Option app on Android (Google Play or APK), iPhone and iPad (web app), Windows and macOS, plus the PocketOption Telegram bot."
  h1="Pocket Option app for every device"
  lead="One account, one balance, every screen. How to install Pocket Option on Android, iPhone, desktop and Telegram, and which version to choose."
  crumb="App"
  toc={toc}
>
  <figure>
    <Image
      src={mobile}
      widths={[360, 640]}
      sizes="(max-width: 640px) 92vw, 360px"
      alt="Pocket Option app on a phone showing a EUR/USD chart"
      style="max-width:360px"
    />
    <figcaption>The Pocket Option mobile platform with an EUR/USD chart and trade panel.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2 id="android">Android</h2>
  <p>
    The Android app is available on <strong>Google Play</strong>. Where Google Play is not available, Pocket Option
    offers an <strong>APK</strong> download from its website. The app supports every trade type, indicators, social
    trading, deposits and withdrawals.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <a href={go("android")} rel="sponsored nofollow">
        Get the Pocket Option app
      </a>{" "}
      from Google Play, or download the APK from the official site.
    </li>
    <li>For the APK, allow installs from your browser when Android asks.</li>
    <li>Log in with your existing account or open the demo.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="iphone">iPhone and iPad</h2>
  <p>
    On iOS, Pocket Option runs as a <strong>web app</strong>. It installs to the home screen and opens full screen like
    a native app.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open{" "}
      <a href={go("app")} rel="sponsored nofollow">
        Pocket Option
      </a>{" "}
      in Safari.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tap the Share button, then <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Launch Pocket Option from the new icon.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="desktop">Windows and macOS</h2>
  <p>
    There is no separate download for desktop. The full platform runs in Chrome, Edge, Safari or Firefox, which keeps it
    up to date automatically and makes it work on any operating system. In Chrome or Edge you can also install it as an
    app from the address bar.
  </p>

  <h2 id="telegram">Telegram bot</h2>
  <p>
    Pocket Option also runs a Telegram bot linked to your account. It is useful for quick checks and notifications on
    the go, while full charting is better on the app or web platform.
  </p>

  <h2 id="compare">Which one to use</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Version</th>
        <th>Best for</th>
        <th>Install</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Web platform</td>
        <td>Analysis on a large screen</td>
        <td>None</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Android app</td>
        <td>Trading on the go</td>
        <td>Google Play or APK</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>iOS web app</td>
        <td>iPhone and iPad users</td>
        <td>Add to Home Screen</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Telegram bot</td>
        <td>Quick checks, alerts</td>
        <td>Open in Telegram</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Not sure yet?{" "}
    <a href={go("demo")} rel="sponsored nofollow">
      Open the demo
    </a>{" "}
    on your phone and desktop and see which you prefer.
  </p>
</Article>
